 individual referee fixed effects or referee-country implicit bias scores, despite these being available in the data", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee fixed effects", "implicit bias scores"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 117, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[130, 130]], "note": "general caveat about possible unaddressed team/club effects"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[131, 131]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[132, 133]], "note": "caveat about subjective/photo-based skin tone measurement and possible misclassification"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[134, 134]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[135, 136]], "assertion": "descriptive checks comparing red card rates between excluded (missing-data) and included dyads showed similar rates, offered as mitigating selection-bias concern from the 21% exclusion", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["selection bias", "exclusion comparison"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[137, 137]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[138, 139]], "note": "generalizability caveat limited to European soccer 2012–2013"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[140, 140]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[141, 141]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[142, 142]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[143, 143]], "assertion": "the use of standard, non-clustered SEs is characterized as a methodological choice aligned with the exploratory advocacy posture", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["standard errors", "advocacy posture"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[145, 145]], "assertion": "argument that conditional independence given covariates makes clustering conservative if covariates capture most player/referee heterogeneity", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conditional independence argument"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[146, 146]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[147, 147]], "assertion": "argument that standard SEs are defensible under a design-based inference view treating the dataset itself as the population of interest", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["design-based inference argument"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[148, 148]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[149, 149]], "assertion": "restates that the GEE player-clustering sensitivity analysis gave qualitatively similar results with wider CIs, taken as confirming robustness", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["GEE sensitivity analysis"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[150, 150]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[151, 151]], "note": "appeal to precedent in the sports-analytics literature for using standard SEs, not a claim about this analysis' own actions"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[153, 153]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[154, 154]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[155, 155]], "assertion": "the cutpoint was chosen to maximize the effect, and the authors assert this choice is nonetheless justifiable", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cutpoint selection"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[156, 156]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "argument that 0.25 has substantive meaning as the boundary between 'very light skin' and all other categories", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cutpoint meaning"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[158, 158]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "the 40.5%/59.5% light/dark split is argued to provide adequate sample size in both groups", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample balance"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[161, 161]], "assertion": "the effect is also present, though weaker, at other cutpoints and in continuous specifications, indicating it is not solely an artifact of dichotomization", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness", "cutpoint"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[162, 162]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "the cutpoint optimization is stated to be fully disclosed so readers can evaluate alternative cutpoints", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["transparency"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[164, 164]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[165, 165]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[167, 167]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "the analysis is said to provide strong directional support for the referee-bias hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 174]], "assertion": "restates the primary RD (0.25pp, CI [0.11,0.39], p=0.0006) and OR (1.22, CI [1.09,1.37], p=0.0005) estimates", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "the effect is described as consistent across multiple sensitivity analyses, covariate adjustments, and sample definitions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[176, 176]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "the effect is characterized as statistically significant and substantively meaningful, representing consequential disparate treatment", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion", "significance"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 161, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "listed strength: large sample of 112,853 dyads, 1,405 players, 2,882 referees", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[182, 182]], "assertion": "listed strength: high-quality measurement via reliable skin tone ratings (r=0.92) and an objective outcome", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["measurement quality"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[183, 183]], "assertion": "listed strength: covariate adjustment controls for key confounders (exposure, anthropometrics, league)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate adjustment"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "listed strength: the effect is stable across multiple specifications", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[185, 185]], "assertion": "listed strength: full reproducibility with complete code and documentation provided", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[187, 187]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[189, 189]], "assertion": "the analysis had no pre-registration and no out-of-sample validation", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["pre-registration", "out-of-sample validation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [173]}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[189, 189]], "assertion": "specification search was used, framed here as a named limitation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["specification search"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [172]}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "general caveat that unmeasured confounding (e.g. player aggression) cannot be ruled out"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "restates as a limitation that the cutpoint was chosen to maximize the effect, while continuous specifications show weaker but still significant effects", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cutpoint selection"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 176, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[192, 192]], "assertion": "standard errors were not clustered for player/referee correlation, which may underestimate uncertainty", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[193, 193]], "note": "generalizability limitation restated"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[194, 194]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[195, 195]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "states the exploratory analysis motivates future confirmatory work"}, {"id": 182, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[198, 198]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[199, 204]], "note": "recommended future/confirmatory research steps not carried out in this analysis"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[205, 205]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[206, 206]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[208, 211]], "note": "speculative ethical/policy implications contingent on future replication"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[212, 212]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[214, 214]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[215, 215]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[216, 216]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[217, 224]], "assertion": "all analyses are reproducible from the provided Python script and dataset, which include data QC, exclusion criteria, cutpoint testing, the primary logistic model, marginal effect computation, and four sensitivity analyses", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility", "analysis script"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[225, 225]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "a random seed of 42 was set for reproducibility of any stochastic operations", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [196]}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "no stochastic operations were actually used in the final models", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["stochastic operations"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [195]}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[227, 227]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[228, 228]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[229, 229]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 200, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[230, 230]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[231, 231]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[232, 232]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 203, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[233, 235]], "assertion": "restates the primary risk difference estimate 0.0025 (0.25pp), 95% CI [0.0011,0.0039], p=0.0006", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 204, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[236, 236]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 205, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[237, 237]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 206, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[238, 239]], "assertion": "restates the secondary odds ratio estimate 1.223, 95% CI [1.091,1.371]", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[240, 240]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[241, 241]], "note": "subsection heading"}, {"id": 209, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[242, 243]], "assertion": "restates unit of analysis (player-referee dyad) and N (112,853 dyads, 1,405 players, 2,882 referees)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["unit of analysis", "sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 210, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[244, 244]], "assertion": "restates covariates used: log(games), age, height, weight, league country", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariates"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 211, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[245, 245]], "assertion": "restates exclusion counts: missing skin tone (21,407), missing anthropometrics (753), goalkeepers (11,015)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 212, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[246, 246]], "assertion": "restates transformations applied: skin tone dichotomized at 0.25, log(games), standardized age/height/weight", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["transformations"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 213, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[247, 247]], "assertion": "restates that the SE method used was standard logit, not clustered", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 214, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[248, 248]], "assertion": "no weighting was used", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["weighting"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 215, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[249, 249]], "assertion": "no fixed effects were used; league country was included only as a categorical covariate", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["fixed effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 216, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[250, 250]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 217, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[251, 251]], "assertion": "the conclusion is stated as SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 218, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[252, 252]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 219, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[253, 253]], "assertion": "final conclusion: the hypothesis is supported, with a statistically significant and substantively meaningful 0.25pp (23% relative) increase in adjusted red card risk for dark-skinned players, robust to multiple sensitivity analyses and covariate adjustments", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [220]}, {"id": 220, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[253, 253]], "assertion": "the findings are explicitly characterized as an upper bound on evidence, given the exploratory in-sample analysis with specification search, requiring confirmation via preregistered out-of-sample research", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["evidentiary status", "confirmatory research"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [219]}, {"id": 221, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[254, 255]], "note": "blank lines"}, {"id": 222, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[256, 256]], "note": "tool-output wrapper closing tag"}]}}